    "date": "22-10-12",
    "author": "By Vikas Kumar",
    "image": "/images/blog/6351diploma-programs_cms-ed-1.png",
    "content": "<p>Diploma in Community Medical Service and Essential Drugs (CMS &amp; ED) course is 1.5years program with 2 semesters+ 6month training. CMS &amp; ED Diploma Course is for practicing in the sector of primary Health Care by general allopathic medicines which are approved by world health organization (WHO) for primaryhealth care. The Hon. Supreme Court of India has given an order that CMS &amp; ED</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Diploma holder can practice in allopathic prescription for all diseases includingn Infection diseases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Medical professionals holding degree with BEMS, BHMS, BAMS, BUMS,</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Naturopathy, Alternative Medicines, Psychology, EMO Doctors who wants to</p>\r\n\r\n<p>practice in Allopathy medicines can opt for CMS&amp;ED Diploma course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>CAREER</strong> <strong>OPTION</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Community Health Worker</li>\r\n\t<li>Rural Medical Officer</li>\r\n\t<li>&nbsp;General Physician</li>\r\n\t<li>Health Physician</li>\r\n\t<li>Dietician</li>\r\n\t<li>Psychologist (with Ph.D. Psychology)</li>\r\n\t<li>Emergency Health Physician in Rural Areas</li>\r\n\t<li>Assistant Doctor</li>\r\n\t<li>&nbsp;Assistant Pharmacist</li>\r\n\t<li>&nbsp;Primary Health Care</li>\r\n\t<li>&nbsp;Generic Medicines</li>\r\n\t<li>Allopathic Practitioner</li>\r\n</ul>"
